{"title":"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(No_Fibonacci)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (No Fibonacci)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Fibbonacci)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Fibbonacci)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Straightforward)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Straightforward)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_DDM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by DDM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Squares of side length 1, 1, 2, 3, and 5 are arranged to form the rectangle shown below. A curve is drawn by inscribing a quarter circle in each square and joining the quarter circles in order, from shortest to longest. What is the length of the curve?\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28No_Fibonacci.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(No_Fibonacci)\">Solution 2 (No Fibonacci)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (No Fibonacci)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For those who don't know Fibonacci's Spiral, One could see that between the two unit squares, the curvature is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/8/b1843fcf60a751ebd04c7e76315f149e43916e74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 2 \\pi (1) = \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"107\" height=\"38\" />. For the unit 2 square, the curve is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f009e9f6d82c8732bf99734f1f8d98584bb2b63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} \\cdot 2 \\pi (2) = \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"107\" height=\"38\" />. For the unit three square, is is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/e/b6eb70580cfc2d8b77898f598d9a9c32f8ce258d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} \\cdot 2 \\pi (3) = \\frac{3}{2} \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"120\" height=\"38\" />. For the unit 5 square, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/5/235947caa01c61f86f00ff970fbc162e831a6413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} \\cdot 2 \\pi \\cdot 5 = \\frac{10}{4} \\pi = \\frac{5}{2} \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"176\" height=\"38\" />. The length of the curve is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/3/9a39dc2becfc65a1eaadf926af79389e5252d29e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi + \\frac{8}{2} \\pi = 2\\pi + 4\\pi = \\boxed{6\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"211\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Fibbonacci.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Fibbonacci)\">Solution 3 (Fibbonacci)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Fibbonacci)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For those who know Fibonacci's Spiral, the length of the curve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/9/6a9ae9ef661c78749ead3c680be4f2be24b15d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_n = \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\sum_{k=1}^n F_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"114\" height=\"53\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/f/d8f60ea5bcead88beedbd19d4e75f9272ea75193.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />th Fibonacci Number. Here, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is the number of squares the curve traverses. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd85763388384ff2c3dd9d896d0e77a2d92ed1ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L_5 = \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\cdot (12) = \\boxed{6 \\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"162\" height=\"34\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Straightforward.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Straightforward)\">Solution 4 (Straightforward)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Straightforward)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the circumference of a quarter arc is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/c/e8c7ccfa2f74ebb567accd6920c20c2a5dbbe0f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} \\cdot 2 \\cdot \\pi \\cdot r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"83\" height=\"38\" />\nWhich is the same thing as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/c/fbca29b15e0fe83f5fd02c7d4f7449658b507249.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {1}{2} \\cdot \\pi \\cdot r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"61\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>The first part of the spiral has a quarter circle with the radius of 5 and so the formula would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/7/c7714899b6ca54a5b52d7bb06540ea88e74e1c13.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\pi \\cdot 5 = \\frac{5}{2}\\pi\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>The second part of the spiral has a quarter circle with the radius of 3 and so the formula is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/0/870891d5e22a4099c9eed1495df815f0e9114229.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\pi \\cdot 3 = \\frac{3}{2}\\pi\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>The third part of the spiral has a quarter circle with the radius of 2 and so the formula is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/c/b1c218eefa69d0eb900f00c5740172499de0900b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\pi\\cdot2 = \\pi\\]\" width=\"92\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>The fourth and fifth part can be viewed as 2 quarter circles with radius 1, so they are essentially one semicircle with radius 1. The formula then would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e578d1a6850cc401e7cf09aab4775ec05f8cca58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 2 \\cdot r = \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"118\" height=\"38\" /> Therefore, it is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />. \n</p><p>Adding them all up, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/e/5be10332635c42851aa68063b3ed463a14ee8f49.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{5}{2}\\pi + \\frac{3}{2}\\pi + 1\\pi +1\\pi = \\frac{8}{2}\\pi + 2\\pi = 6\\pi\\]\" width=\"287\" height=\"38\" />\nTherefore our final answer is  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/c/35ce60e90ff1c1b7dd763bece2ce2020966dfd06.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{6\\pi}.\\]\" width=\"35\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>-Razorpro10\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/gzXlOkLl24U\">https://youtu.be/gzXlOkLl24U</a>\n</p><p>~TheSmartGreekMathDude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_DDM\">Video Solution by DDM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by DDM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/nY1hhVbEeBk\">https://youtu.be/nY1hhVbEeBk</a>\n</p><p>~piggydude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Thinking Feet\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/5GiqtDlVDdg\">https://youtu.be/5GiqtDlVDdg</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3GmtxMC-W1I&amp;t=1072s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3GmtxMC-W1I&amp;t=1072s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1tVME6REUp/\">https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1tVME6REUp/</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8\" title=\"2026 AMC 8\">2026 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2026\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n